save(63,dict(paragraphs=["Harinder Cheema is a poet and author whose books include The Temple Stop and Soul Chants. In an interview about her writing, she spoke of literature’s relationship with society and of the need to look beyond personal gain towards a shared good.","‘At the Time of Homecoming’, her poem in Kabita Live, imagines earthly life as a school day and the Creator as a parent waiting at home. Its familiar images of play, rules and a clean uniform frame a moral question: what kind of life will we have lived when it is time to return?"],sources=[source('Harinder Cheema — author interview, Polis Magazino','https://www.polismagazino.gr/harinder-cheema-literature-is-a-mirror-to-life-and-society/',['Author names The Temple Stop and Soul Chants; literature/society and collective good'])],identity_match='Both distinctive book titles match captured biography; signed interview identifies same author.',poems_read=[dict(id=48,title='At The Time Of Homecoming',basis='Full original read: school/playground allegory, divine parent, desire and unstained uniform on returning home.')],limitations=['Only-Indian and complete-work award claims omitted because award-organiser evidence not checked.','Promotional rankings, achievement-list claims and anthology totals omitted.','No verified direct book product page added.','Poem allegory described without inferring a personal religious affiliation.'],next_action='Independent author/editor review; optional organiser verification of awards.'))
